Stathol Turris <stathol@hotmail.com> wrote:
>I can think of a few problems with that approach, though. For one,
>an observant player might be able to tell in advance that they are
>going to receive a bones file by watching the size of their save.

Surely this is cheating anyway? If you're watching the size of your save
file, it's not that big a step to looking inside it for interesting
facts like which objects are which. Also, if you're poking around inside
nethack's state directory at all, you can trivially see which bones
files may be generated because their file names contain the level
number, and so the same observant player could make strategic decisions
about which branch to follow in the early game based on which potential
bones files exist.

Me, I stay the heck out of /var/games/nethack/ unless I'm debugging
something.

